Follow-up from code review of the trailing-slash fix. Grepped all Rust callers for /api/.../ paths: desktop profiles.rs had the same bug (its fake-server test asserted the broken path, so it could never catch it); remote_auth.rs and the connect callback test probed unrouted slash paths, so they passed on SPA/404 responses without touching the routes they meant to test. Declined two review suggestions: (1) moving the API 404 into a nested-router .fallback — the internal listener merges two separate nest("/api") routers, and axum rejects merging routers that both carry fallbacks, so the shared SPA fallback is the one place that sees every unmatched /api path; (2) the 404-vs-401 pre-auth distinction — unknown paths already returned 200 HTML vs 401 before this change, so no new route-existence signal is exposed. Ran: server 188, tauri 36, cli remote_auth 6, all pass.
